-- Whether a ball's "target" attribute refers to the local player. The attribute
-- is not always the plain Name — depending on the game version it can be the
-- DisplayName or the UserId (and can be a number, not a string). The old
-- `target == tostring(LocalPlayer)` only matched the Name, so on any version that
-- used a different form the parry thought no ball was targeting you and never
-- fired. Normalise to a string and accept Name / DisplayName / UserId.
local function BallTargetsMe(t)
    if t == nil then return false end
    local lp = ACHAOTICDATA.Player.LocalPlayer
    local ts = tostring(t)
    return ts == lp.Name or ts == lp.DisplayName or ts == tostring(lp.UserId)
end

